description: Route backend work to the shared backend instruction file and follow existing architecture and extension patterns
globs:
  - backend/**/*.py
  - backend/**/*.json
  - backend/**/*.md
  - backend/run.sh
  - backend/.env.example
  - readme.md
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the full-stack parent instructions first, then the backend child instructions whenever the task involves backend code, tests, runtime configuration, backend docs, or architecture decisions.

For backend feature requests, the parent instructions include a mandatory clarification-first workflow:

- ask 3 important questions when the request is ambiguous
- confirm or recommend API inputs and outputs before implementation
- reuse an existing module/use case when relevant
- implement with strict DTOs, services, and thin controllers
- optimize with shared concerns like caching, idempotency, retries, timeouts, request tracing, and rate limiting when relevant
- prefer practical task or workflow endpoints over generic sample routes when the product direction calls for them
- add tests under `backend/tests/`
- document the feature in the same use-case area when possible

For backend documentation work, prefer Mermaid-first architecture docs with concise supporting text.

Read and follow:

@.cursor/fullstack-agentic-flow.md
@.cursor/backend-agentic-flow.md
